THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-21, part 3) — federate the CRM to the tenant's Keycloak
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Added: a Keycloak (OIDC) provider for Relaticle's Socialite seam and the two
public routes that drive a federated sign-in, so the CRM accepts the SAME
identity that signs the brand into the platform console — the tenant's own
Keycloak realm `tenant-<slug>` — instead of a brokered stored credential.

Reason: the previous session broker minted a one-time Relaticle login from a
platform-held identity. The operator decision (2026-10-20) is to FEDERATE each
module to Keycloak OIDC rather than broker a session, so this replaces the CRM
half with a real Authorization Code + PKCE round trip against the tenant's realm.
Relaticle is one deployment serving every tenant, so the realm is not a
deployment-wide `config/services.php` client: it is named per request
(`{workspace}` whose slug is the realm suffix), which is what makes the
federation per-tenant rather than one shared login.

