THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-28, part 7) — the platform contact field set
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Added: a fixed contact schema every workspace is seeded with — 25 codes in three
bands (identity and channel handles, profile, and the five consent mirrors), the
one place that builds its field and option rows, and a backfill for the
workspaces that predate a code.

Reason: upstream lets a workspace author its own custom fields through Filament
and starts every workspace with only the four built-in contact columns, so no
schema is guaranteed to exist twice. An orchestrator writing contacts for many
tenants would have to discover each workspace's fields before it could write
one. This field set is the contract instead: the same codes, types and options in
every workspace, seeded on creation and backfilled into the ones already there.

