THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-29, part 10) - credential reissue for an existing workspace
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Added: `POST /api/v1/workspaces/{slug}/token`, guarded by the same X-Platform-Key
shared secret as the provisioning route; and two fields (`owner_email`,
`owner_changed`) on the session broker's response.

Reason: the platform stores the plaintext of the workspace-pinned Sanctum token it
is given at creation, and this application keeps only its SHA-256. So when the
session broker adopts a workspace onto the tenant's own identity
(`EnsureWorkspaceOwner`, the only writer of `workspaces.user_id`), the stored
credential is left signing as an identity that neither owns nor belongs to that
workspace, and SetApiWorkspaceContext answers 403 "You do not belong to this
workspace." on every workspace-scoped route, permanently. There was no way to mint
a replacement for a workspace that already existed, so the calling platform could
not repair it either. Measured on the platform: 26 of 32 credentialed tenants held
a token minted for the shared service user, i.e. each one died at its first
adoption.

The new route mints for the workspace's OWNER OF RECORD (never an identity the
caller names) with the same abilities and the same workspace pin the provisioning
route uses, and retires the workspace's earlier `platform:<slug>` tokens in the
same call, minting first so a failed reissue cannot leave the caller
credential-less.

Files added:
  app/Actions/Platform/IssueWorkspaceToken.php
      the ONE mint implementation (owner abilities + workspace_id pin + retire of
      the tokens it replaces); ProvisionWorkspace::mintWorkspaceToken now delegates
      to it
  app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/WorkspaceTokenController.php
      POST /api/v1/workspaces/{slug}/token
  tests/Feature/Platform/WorkspaceTokenReissueTest.php

Files changed:
  app/Actions/Platform/ProvisionWorkspace.php      delegates the mint
  app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/WorkspaceSessionController.php
      reports owner_email and owner_changed, so the caller that holds the plaintext
      knows when the adoption moved ownership and its credential must be replaced
  routes/api.php        registers POST /api/v1/workspaces/{slug}/token
  tests/Feature/Platform/WorkspaceSessionBrokerTest.php

Upstream behaviour is unchanged: no existing route, ability or pin changes, and a
workspace created or adopted exactly as before still answers exactly as it did.


THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-29, part 11) - the lifecycle_stage correction pass compares
                                      every contact instead of trusting a cursor
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Changed: `LifecycleStageReconciler` and the `platform:reconcile-lifecycle-stages`
command (the `*/5` schedule entry and its `03:40 --full`). No route, model, migration
or schema is touched.

Reason: `lifecycle_stage` is derived from the contact's deals, and the correction pass
that repairs a value written behind the application selected contacts by timestamp -
`opportunities.updated_at`, and `activity_log` rows about an opportunity, since
`cursor - 600s`. A `custom_field_values` row carries no timestamps at all and a write
straight into Postgres fires no audit trigger, so such a value produced neither, was
invisible to the five-minute tick, and was repaired only by the nightly full sweep.
Measured on the platform's dev host (2026-10-28, two contacts corrupted at the same
instant): the one whose deals had moved inside the window came back on the next tick;
the one whose deal had last been touched six days earlier was still wrong after two
ticks and was fixed only when a human ran `--full`.

The pass now COMPARES: every live contact's stored value against the stage its live
opportunities justify, writing only the contacts that disagree. Three queries per
workspace (stored values, derived answer, contacts with no usable value row) and one
write per wrong contact. The rule itself is still `LifecycleStage::fromOpportunityStages()`
and nothing else, so the detector and the writer cannot disagree. The per-tick work is
bounded by `--budget` (default 5000 contacts; whole workspaces are deferred and counted,
never half-swept) and `--full` is the same pass with no budget. The cursor row is still
written as an observability high-water mark and gates nothing.

Files changed:
  app/Support/LifecycleStage/LifecycleStageReconciler.php
      `touchedContacts()` (both cursor legs) and its `activity_log` query are removed;
      `driftSet()` + `write()` replace the chunked walk of every contact; `storedStages()`
      joins `people` with `deleted_at IS NULL`; `contactsWithoutAStageValue()` is new
  app/Console/Commands/ReconcileLifecycleStagesCommand.php
      `--budget`, and an output line that reports contacts compared, corrected and
      workspaces not visited
  bootstrap/app.php                       the schedule entries and their comment
  tests/Feature/LifecycleStage/LifecycleStageTest.php
      the tick case (a cursor in place, both old legs outside their window), the
      no-value-row case, the soft-deleted case, the deferral case, idempotency

Upstream behaviour is unchanged for every path that reads the field: the observers
still write it inside the write, the guard still refuses a hand edit, and a derived
change still writes no `activity_log` row.


